# 7. Security Consideration

In AWS, an EC2 instance normally uses a **Security Group** to control inbound traffic.

For example:

```text
Inbound Rule

Protocol: TCP
Port: 22
Source: Jenkins Server
```

Our local VMware environment does not have AWS Security Groups.

Therefore, we reproduced the concept using the Ubuntu firewall, UFW.

On VM2:

```bash
sudo ufw status
```

SSH access can be restricted to VM1's IP:

```bash
sudo ufw allow from VM1_IP to any port 22 proto tcp
```

For example:

```bash
sudo ufw allow from 192.168.146.137 to any port 22 proto tcp
```

This gives us an important real-world security principle:

> The deployment server should not unnecessarily expose SSH to everybody.

