# 24. Mapping the Lab to AWS

One of the most important learning outcomes is understanding how the local environment maps to AWS.

| Local VMware Lab       | AWS Equivalent                       |
| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| VM1                    | Jenkins/CI server                    |
| VM2                    | EC2 instance                         |
| VMware private network | VPC/private networking concept       |
| VM2 private IP         | EC2 private IP                       |
| UFW                    | Security Group-like firewall control |
| SSH                    | SSH into EC2                         |
| SSH key                | EC2 key-pair authentication          |
| Docker Engine          | Docker on EC2                        |
| Docker Hub             | ECR/Container Registry               |
| Jenkins                | CI/CD automation server              |
| Docker image           | Deployable application artifact      |
| Browser → VM2:3080     | Browser → EC2:application-port       |

This is not a literal replacement for AWS infrastructure. Rather, it is a **local simulation of the deployment architecture and workflow**.

