# 28. Lessons Learned

The project demonstrates several important DevOps principles.

### Principle 1 — Separate Build From Deployment

The machine that builds the application does not have to be the machine that runs it.

```text
VM1 = Build
VM2 = Deploy
```

### Principle 2 — Use an Artifact Registry

Docker Hub provides a central location for the image.

```text
Build → Registry → Deployment
```

### Principle 3 — Automate Deployment

Instead of manually copying files to VM2, Jenkins performs the deployment.

### Principle 4 — Use SSH Securely

SSH provides secure communication between Jenkins and the deployment server.

### Principle 5 — Control Network Access

Only required ports should be exposed.

### Principle 6 — Build Once, Deploy the Same Artifact

The image built and tested by Jenkins is the same image deployed to VM2.

This reduces the possibility of differences between the build environment and deployment environment.

