# 29. Possible Improvements

The current laboratory can be extended further.

### Versioned Docker Images

Instead of using:

```text
latest
```

we use:

```text
1.1.9-6
```

This gives us traceability.

For example:

```text
1.1.9-5
1.1.9-6
1.1.9-7
```

We can identify exactly which version is deployed.

### Automated Rollback

If version `1.1.9-7` fails:

```text
1.1.9-7
    ↓
FAIL
    ↓
Rollback
    ↓
1.1.9-6
```

### Health Checks

Jenkins can verify that the application is actually running after deployment.

For example:

```bash
curl http://192.168.146.138:3080
```

### Docker Compose

The deployment can eventually be moved from:

```bash
docker run
```

to:

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

### Nginx

We can introduce Nginx as a reverse proxy:

```text
Browser
   ↓
Nginx :80
   ↓
Application :8080
```

### HTTPS

We can eventually add TLS/HTTPS.

### Kubernetes

The same container image could later be deployed to Kubernetes.

